; Plan 07, "IT, inline": a cell moved to a tick that is not a row start
; uses `SDx` — delay x ticks — when the delta fits and the cell has no
; effect column. The cell at row 2 carries none, and 5 765 760 ticks is
; three of the twenty-four a row holds at speed 24, so the move is `SD3`
; in the row it already sits in.
; The echo carries `anchor_unavailable`: the anchor names a file that is
; not beside this document, and plan 02 says so out loud rather than
; silently honouring an offset. Nothing here depends on it — the tier is
; INLINE and every event the plan touches is in the text above — and the
; diagnostic is in the golden because a document that claims a file it
; does not have is a fact worth seeing.
(plan retime :args (a :sel (s :lanes [lead] :kinds [note] :range [92252160 92252161]) :delta 5765760))
